# Install on this Mac after commit and push

When you commit and push **Grok & Cursor Usage**, finish on this Mac. Do not ask Kevin to pull, build, or install.

1. `git pull origin` for the branch you just pushed, so this checkout matches Origin.
2. Build the Mac app:

```bash
xcodebuild -project GrokCursorUsage.xcodeproj -scheme GrokCursorUsage \
  -configuration Debug \
  -derivedDataPath /tmp/GrokCursorUsageDerivedData \
  -destination 'platform=macOS' \
  -allowProvisioningUpdates build
```

3. Quit **Grok & Cursor Usage** if it is running.
4. Replace `/Applications/Grok & Cursor Usage.app` with the built app and launch that copy.
5. Use `/tmp/GrokCursorUsageDerivedData`. Never put DerivedData inside iCloud.

Skip the build only when this machine has no `xcodebuild`.
